shape theory.algebra : theory.emergence.general-composition, theory.minimal, theory.landscape {
  type: definition
  layer: 0
  """
// Section 16 (The Algebra of Shapes).
//
// 16.1 Structural Equivalence (Def 16.1): A ~= B when a
// correspondence preserves transformation and reference.
// Reflexive, symmetric, transitive.
//
// 16.2 Identity Element (Thm 16.3): under identity structure,
// empty_s is the identity for composition: A compose empty_s ~= A.
//
// 16.3 Continuity as Structure (Thm 16.4): continuity across
// transformation IS structure S. Two moments belong to the same
// shape iff they share the same structure.
// Corollary 16.4a (Identity): a shape's identity is its complete
// trace: structure + character together.
//
// 16.4 Structural Change (Def 16.5): structural continuity
// requires a chain of intermediates where each differs in at most
// one structural feature. Structural distance is the minimum
// chain length (Def 16.7).
//
// 16.5 Mixing angle of structural change (Thm 16.8).
//
// 16.6 Dual Perspective (Thm 16.11): individual vs system
// perspective. Neither reducible to the other.
//
// 16.7 Cross-Perspective Coherence (Thm 16.12): the two
// perspectives must be mutually coherent.
//
// Derives from: theory.emergence.general-composition,
//               theory.minimal, theory.landscape
  """
}
